#Bach Brandenberg no 2 in F major arranged for Sonic Pi by Robin Newman August 2016
#I started with an existing score in MuseScore and modified it from 10 parts into 17 parts
#so that it could be accommodated by Sonic Pi. The individual parts were then exported
# in MusicXML format and coverted using a script into SP notation.
#In this version the parts are played with built in SP synths
#Flute on :beep, Oboe and Trumpet on :tri, Clavichord (8 parts) on :pulse
#Solo Violin on :beep, string orchestrs V1,V2,Vila,Cello,Bass on :saw
#part levels and pan positions are adjusted so that the rich interplay texture
#cam be heard, and reverb is added to the whole.
#Some of the Clavichord aprts only have two or three notes, but because of the timings
#separate parts are needed to accommodate them.
#The file is so long that it requires the run_file command introduced in
# Sonic Pi 2.11dev to play it. 

